{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Make for yourself.</b> Like the form of a seraph serpent of copper, for thus it is written." "<b>On a standard.</b> That it be high, and all see it. Many went astray and said that this form receives power from supernal beings — far be it, far be it, for the thing was done by the command of HaShem, and it is not for us to seek why the form of a serpent. And if not so, let him show us: is there a tree that sweetens bitter waters? Even honey does not sweeten them. And what reason to place a fig-cake on a boil? And it is not in the nature of the fig-cake to remove the boil. And the truth is that the knowledge of the Supernal is exalted beyond us."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:38.555361201Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}